{"kind":"assert","text":"Order of the client and MCP boundary lane, NF-1 to NF-5. Hugh said as\nsoon as possible for this work on 11 November, so I change one line of\nNF-1 6050f6ea.\n\n- NF-1 6050f6ea, neutral `Form`.\n- NF-2 9a321a0a, the MCP boundary and one typed act result.\n- NF-3 dd0d078a, custody moves to the client.\n- NF-4 d2aff067, the command line installs with no MCP service.\n- NF-5 c288c917, the browser on the one custody. After the cutover.\n\nNF-1 to NF-4 no longer wait for the identifier cutover head. They wait\nonly for S4 9a053402, which edits the same MCP files and is older.\nStart their source now in one lane, each head on the one before it.\nEach takes the gate slot when it is ready and the slot is free. The\ncutover head integrates main as these land, as it does for JP1, OPS-1\nand S1.\n\nGate order when two heads are ready at once: JP1, S1, S4, NF-1, NF-2,\nNF-3, NF-4. The cutover head takes the slot whenever it is ready, ahead\nof the NF heads.\n\nThe planner deploys after each landing that changes a Worker bundle.\n`MCP_ENABLED` stays off until S4 lands.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}